# Cargo's build directory. Everything cargo generates lives under here,
# including MSVC .pdb files and criterion's benchmark output, so neither
# needs a rule of its own.
target

# rustfmt's --backup mode writes these next to the source it rewrote.
**/*.rs.bk

# rustc dumps an internal-compiler-error report into the working
# directory, not into target/.
rustc-ice-*.txt

# Python writes its bytecode cache beside any module it imports.
__pycache__/

# Local runtime state, at the paths the binary uses when nothing
# overrides them. Created the moment it runs, and holding real secrets:
# smeltr-leader-data has this leader's TLS private key and its SQLite
# database, smeltr-worker-data a worker's persisted bearer credential.
#
# Deliberately not anchored to the repo root. These paths are relative to
# whatever directory the binary was started in, so running one from a
# subdirectory of a checkout puts those secrets there instead -- where a
# root-anchored rule would not cover them.
smeltr-leader-data/
smeltr-worker-data/

# A real startup config (smeltr.example.toml stays checked in as the
# template) can carry real hostnames or a worker's one-time enrollment
# code. Same reasoning as above, including why it is not anchored.
smeltr.toml

# A leader generates this on first use; it opens every stored value and is never committed.
smeltr-leader-secrets/

# `just dist` writes these: a stripped binary of tens of megabytes, the
# files that package and run it, and the tarball of all three. Every one
# derives from this checkout.
handoff/
smeltr-*.tar
smeltr-*.tar.gz
smeltr-*.tar.gz.sha256
smeltr-*.zip
SHA256SUMS

# `just stig` and `just cves` write their reports here.
stig/
cves/
sbom/
